Z||000000||Babygirl||10-11-2000||10:48 PM||||Great.  Now since my windshield wipers quit working, my odometer and speedometer don't work.  Help!  Is it just a loose or broken cable?  How difficult is this to replace?<P>Please help.  I love my car ...<P>------------------<BR>~Darcy & Laura<BR>1984 Black SE Fiero||||reg||9
Z||000001||StuGood||10-11-2000||10:59 PM||||Maybe the speedometer is set up to give you the speed of your wipers  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"><P>Between this and your wiper trouble, sounds like it's time to start looking for (a) loose connector(s).  Check your fuses also.<P>The speedometer is electrical - there's no cable to mess with.  Start by checking the connector at the speedometer sending unit, which is plugged into the transaxle.  Next you might check the connector which plugs into bottom LHS of the instrument panel.<P>Electrical problems can be frustrating, but don't give up.  You will eventually get it. <BR> ||||reg||12
